At Tue, 12 Jun 2007 15:27:30 +0530,
Nobin Mathew wrote:
> 
> In ubuntu this script mutes all mixer controls.
> 
> So there will be no noise (pop/clicks) during shutdown.
> 
> since I am writing an ASoC driver, it is better to provide shutdown
> vector which will shutdown the system properly.
> 
> If SIGTERM is handled properly in the application then this is also
> not needed, in this case closing the substream will take care of
> proper shutdown (DAPM)
> 
> But we need to take care of applications which will not handle SIGTERM properly.

Yeah, I understand it would be good for some rare cases.
The patch will be welcome, as usual :)


thanks,

